WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:05.240
If you like action movies and you also like
genre stories that dig into one key conceptual

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.380
hook and its many implications along the way,
The Old Guard is a film for you.

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:13.220
From how it wraps up to where it might go
next, this is the ending of The Old Guard

00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:13.800
explained.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.800
Here's your warning: spoilers ahead for The
Old Guard.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:23.300
The chief threat of The Old Guard is Merrick,
a pharmaceutical tycoon who becomes convinced

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:26.620
that Andy and her near-immortal crew are the
key to opening up all sorts of pathways to

00:00:26.620 --> 00:00:30.800
curing disease, slowing the aging process,
and perhaps even stopping death.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:35.980
Merrick has vast financial resources, tremendous
tenacity, and the help of Copley's research.

00:00:36.700 --> 00:00:41.220
He also has Booker's help, and with all of
that at his back he's very nearly able to

00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:44.320
capture and incapacitate every single member
of the Old Guard.

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:48.320
Of course, by the end of the film Merrick
has fallen out of his own skyscraper with

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.780
an axe in his neck, so he won't be coming
after them again any time soon.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.399
That said, as Andy notes near the end of the
film, it's almost impossible to stay hidden

00:00:56.400 --> 00:00:57.760
in the modern world they live in.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:02.800
If Merrick was able to track them down and
deploy his wealth to very nearly cage them

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.600
all, who's to say an even wealthier business
tycoon somewhere can't do the same, particularly

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:09.340
after they learn about what Merrick went through?

00:01:09.740 --> 00:01:13.000
All it takes is one person with knowledge
of the team who's willing to say what they

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:13.260
know.

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.600
When we first meet Nile, she's an American
Marine just trying to do her best who discovers

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.160
quite by accident that she's immortal.

00:01:20.890 --> 00:01:25.120
Much of the film's emotional core is devoted
to Nile coming to terms with her abilities

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.880
and the massive implications they have, including
what it means for her relationship with her

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:29.620
loved ones.

00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.740
As the other members of the Old Guard explain,
if she tries to keep in touch with her family

00:01:33.940 --> 00:01:36.520
and stay with them until they die, they'll
grow to resent her.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:43.140
"And you will never forget the hate and despair
in their eyes."

00:01:44.100 --> 00:01:48.360
Still, Nile persists in her desire to keep
in contact with her family, to the point that

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.700
Andy even relents and gives her back her phone.

00:01:51.140 --> 00:01:55.470
In the end, Nile chooses her new family of
immortals, but reveals in the final scenes

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:59.590
of the film that she still has her phone,
and therefore still has a lifeline to her

00:01:59.590 --> 00:02:03.020
family even though Copley has promised to
make it look like she was killed in action.

00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:07.750
Though Nile seems content with finding her
way as an immortal, it's very possible she'll

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:11.800
seek out her family again even after her family
learns of her presumed death.

00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:16.620
It's possible she won't be able to resist,
and will open a box that she finds very hard

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:16.880
to close.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:21.280
From the beginning of the film, it's clear
that the Old Guard values their privacy.

00:02:22.030 --> 00:02:26.040
Andy goes so far as to offer to take a photo
for some tourists just so she can delete a

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.680
picture she happened to be in the background
of.

00:02:28.220 --> 00:02:33.140
Then, of course, Copley reveals that he's
been doing research on them going back decades,

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:36.820
complete with photographs, old ID cards, news
clippings, and much more.

00:02:37.280 --> 00:02:41.450
As penance for his attempts to sell them off
to Merrick, she tasks Copley with becoming

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.660
their new eraser of sorts.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:48.100
He will be in charge not just of helping them
coordinate new missions, but of erasing every

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.700
trace that they were there in the first place.

00:02:50.200 --> 00:02:54.300
By the end of the film, the Old Guard has
a new and powerful layer of secrecy in their

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:54.480
corner.

00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.470
Though Merrick is the chief villain of The
Old Guard, he's not alone in his journey to

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:01.200
capturing the crew and learning their secrets.

00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:04.820
Arguably the most important ingredient is
Booker's betrayal.

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.760
Andy and her crew very nearly go down because
her best friend and fellow immortal decides

00:03:09.770 --> 00:03:14.410
it's worth it to turn them all over to medical
researchers in the hope that one day, they'll

00:03:14.410 --> 00:03:15.140
learn how to finally die.

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:20.310
By the end of the film, Andy has found new
purpose in life after her struggle with Merrick,

00:03:20.310 --> 00:03:24.500
and while she shares a part of that with Booker,
the group still votes to punish him by exiling

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:25.240
him from the team.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:28.920
"One hundred years from today they'll meet
you here.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:32.500
Til then you're alone."

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:36.760
But just as he's preparing himself for a lonely
century, Andy's old partner Quynh tracks him

00:03:36.760 --> 00:03:39.960
down, presumably to use him to get to Andy
again.

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:42.760
Booker already betrayed the Old Guard once.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:46.980
With a potential unstable immortal now hunting
him down, will he do it again?

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:50.900
Quynh's return is brief, so there's still
a great deal we don't know about her.

00:03:51.360 --> 00:03:53.260
What we do know is that she's been through
a lot.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:58.530
She suffered a kind of torture that mortal
humans can only imagine, and it probably hasn't

00:03:58.530 --> 00:04:00.040
done anything good for her mental state.

00:04:00.930 --> 00:04:04.280
There's no doubt that she'll at least put
Booker in a difficult position, whatever her

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:05.000
plans may be.

00:04:06.040 --> 00:04:08.040
The members of the Old Guard know they can
die.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:09.040
They just never know when.

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:14.520
Each time they go down in a fight could be
the last, but none of them has any idea what

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.740
triggers that final death, or what the signs
are.

00:04:17.540 --> 00:04:22.160
Near the end of the film, Andy realizes that
she has lost her own grip on immortality when

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:24.340
Booker's shot to her stomach refuses to heal.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:29.040
Though she's apparently now vulnerable enough
that she could be killed, Andy is at peace

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:30.680
by the end of the film.

00:04:31.340 --> 00:04:36.030
She sees her newfound mortality as a tradeoff
for Nile's emergence as the first new immortal

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:37.740
among them in ages.

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:42.120
Seeing her young sister in arms fills her
with a new sense of wonder, and seeing Copley's

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:46.570
research into her past reveals to her that
she has a purpose she can still serve while

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:47.570
she lives.

00:04:47.570 --> 00:04:51.810
So, with all of that in mind, how much longer
does Andy actually have left?

00:04:51.810 --> 00:04:54.690
Will she age conventionally and die in a few
decades?

00:04:54.690 --> 00:04:59.060
Booker seems to think that's the case, though
she seems to know something we don't, telling

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.250
him to have faith.

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:04.780
Is it possible that her lingering gifts could
prolong her life, or even make her somewhat

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.320
harder to kill than a normal human?

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.060
We don't know, but Andy's definitely not done
testing her limits.

00:05:11.480 --> 00:05:14.800
The members of the Old Guard know quite a
lot about how their immortality works.

00:05:15.400 --> 00:05:20.060
They know that it is finite, they know that
they dream of each other when they're apart,

00:05:20.060 --> 00:05:21.500
and they know that they are rare.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.680
What they don't know is why they've been given
these strange gifts and others haven't.

00:05:26.280 --> 00:05:29.040
By the end of the film, though, Copley has
shown them why.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:32.890
In the course of his research into the Old
Guard, he discovers that Andy and her crew

00:05:32.890 --> 00:05:35.260
have a ripple effect on people they save on
missions.

00:05:36.160 --> 00:05:40.280
If they rescue someone, that person's descendants
will do something great in the world, creating

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:43.600
a cumulative good that multiplies the longer
they stay alive.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:48.980
"She saves a life, two or three generations
later we reap the benefits."

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:53.540
This discovery is perhaps the most important
driving factor in the entire film, because

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:56.940
it confirms for Andy that she still has something
worth living for.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.670
The world might be getting worse, but she
has a palpable power to make it better, and

00:06:01.670 --> 00:06:06.370
so the crew sets out at the end with a renewed
sense of purpose, even though they still don't

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:07.220
have all the answers.

